                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Initially, the generated beans will inherit from an abstract base class, and will have standard setters. Getters are modified to check for superseding values or alternative values (if field is null).<br/>
This will have no effect of course if no value providers are registered (through an API of the base class). <br/>
Another deviation from native xjc may be that getters for fields mapped to schema attributes will always be of  the same  type (whether wrapped or unwrapped needs to be decided)  - regardless if they have a default value.
  </td>
