</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      In the demos and test code, the server Impl classes have a WebService annotation that looks like this:<br/>
@javax.jws.WebService(portName = &quot;SoapPort&quot;, serviceName = &quot;SOAPService&quot;, <br/>
                      targetNamespace = &quot;http://apache.org/hello_world_soap_http&quot;, <br/>
                      endpointInterface = &quot;org.apache.hello_world_soap_http.Greeter&quot;)<br/>
<br/>
However, if I code generate a server Impl using the WSDL2Java tool, the &quot;endpointInterface&quot; attribute is missing which causes  a runtime failure.
  </td>
