</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Using CXF as client, Axis as server, Axis throws exception on receiving following message:<br/>
POST /axis/services/Echo HTTP/1.1<br/>
Content-Type: text/xml ; charset=utf-8<br/>
Cache-Control: no-cache<br/>
Pragma: no-cache<br/>
User-Agent: Java/1.5.0_06<br/>
Host: 127.0.0.1:9360<br/>
Accept: text/html, image/gif, image/jpeg, *; q=.2, */*; q=.2<br/>
Connection: keep-alive<br/>
Transfer-Encoding: chunked<br/>
<br/>
e5<br/>
&lt;soap:Envelope xmlns:soap=&quot;http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/&quot;&gt;&lt;soap:Body&gt;&lt;echoBoolean xmlns:ns2=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2005/08/addressing/wsdl&quot; xmlns=&quot;http://soapinterop.org/cxf&quot;&gt;true&lt;/echoBoolean&gt;&lt;/soap:Body&gt;&lt;/soap:Envelope&gt;<br/>
0<br/>
<br/>
Remove the e5 and 0 wrapped on the soap message, then it works. This might relate to the encoding setting in cxf.<br/>

  </td>
