</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      We need the configuration can applied at the server engine level for a given port, for example :<br/>
 <br/>
&lt;bean name=&quot;org.apache.cxf.transport.http.JettyHTTPServerEngine.${http.port}&quot; abstract=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;<br/>
org.apache.cxf.transport.http.JettyHTTPServerEngine is the bean name of the engine, ${http.port} is the specific port. This is useful when there&#39;re multiple types of providers listening on the same port and one wants to apply, say, sslServer properties to all providers. This functionality was available in Celtix, the bean name was different though.<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
