                <tr id="issuerow12362155" rel="12362155" data-issuekey="CXF-410" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-410" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-410">CXF-410</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
            <span class="parentIssue">CXF-316</span>
                specifying exclusions tag in pom.xml can cause issues with ibm jdk
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Sub-task</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Peter Jones
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Peter Jones
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Peter Jones
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 07/Feb/07 00:21 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 29/Aug/07 18:03 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 05/Mar/07 23:26 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0-RC            </td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      <br/>
For instance,  bindings/http/pom.xml has something like this:<br/>
<br/>
    &lt;dependencies&gt;<br/>
        &lt;dependency&gt;<br/>
            &lt;groupId&gt;org.codehaus.jra&lt;/groupId&gt;<br/>
            &lt;artifactId&gt;jra&lt;/artifactId&gt;<br/>
            &lt;version&gt;1.0-alpha-1&lt;/version&gt;<br/>
            &lt;exclusions&gt;<br/>
                &lt;exclusion&gt;<br/>
                    &lt;groupId&gt;junit&lt;/groupId&gt;<br/>
                    &lt;artifactId&gt;junit&lt;/artifactId&gt;<br/>
                &lt;/exclusion&gt;<br/>
            &lt;/exclusions&gt;<br/>
        &lt;/dependency&gt;<br/>
        &lt;dependency&gt;<br/>
            &lt;groupId&gt;junit&lt;/groupId&gt;<br/>
            &lt;artifactId&gt;junit&lt;/artifactId&gt;<br/>
            &lt;scope&gt;test&lt;/scope&gt;<br/>
        &lt;/dependency&gt;<br/>
<br/>
The exclusion of junit from jra - which I believe is meant to prevent junit from being packaged - causes the second junit dependency to be removed with the ibm jdk.  So the tests won&#39;t compile.  The workaround is to comment out the exclusion from the pom.
  </td>
