                <tr id="issuerow12368471" rel="12368471" data-issuekey="CXF-623" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-623" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-623">CXF-623</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                spring bean configuration should support simple wildcards
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Gary Tully
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Gary Tully
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 02/May/07 15:09 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 29/Aug/07 18:09 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 17/May/07 02:53 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.0-RC            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Configuration            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      to apply configuration to a http destination I need to provide the following:<br/>
<br/>
    &lt;bean name=&quot;{http://www.test.com}MyPort.http-destination&quot; abstract=&quot;true&quot;&gt;<br/>
      &lt;property name=&quot;multiplexWithAddress&quot; value=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/bean&gt; <br/>
<br/>
which matches a single port by name.<br/>
I would like to be able to provide<br/>
<br/>
    &lt;bean name=&quot;*.http-destination&quot; abstract=&quot;true&quot;&gt;<br/>
      &lt;property name=&quot;multiplexWithAddress&quot; value=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/bean&gt; <br/>
<br/>
to indicate to apply the config to all http-destinations. To make this work in practice a class attribute is required, otherwise any wildcard would be matched against all beanNames. The package is probably not required in the className attribute.<br/>
<br/>
    &lt;bean name=&quot;*.http-destination&quot; abstract=&quot;true&quot; class=&quot;HttpDestination&quot;&gt;<br/>
      &lt;property name=&quot;multiplexWithAddress&quot; value=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/bean&gt; <br/>
<br/>
To get Spring to merge wildcard and beanName specific config may be a chalenge but it would be great. Possibly it is a case of configuring once with the wildcard match and once with the specific name.<br/>

  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
