                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Because of the current pom.xml, the following are transient compile dependencies of cxf-rt-transports-http:<br/>
- jetty<br/>
- jetty-sslengine<br/>
- jetty-util<br/>
- geronimo-servlet_2.5_spec<br/>
<br/>
This causes the corresponding jars to be copied into WEB-INF/lib for WARs that use the CXFServlet.<br/>
<br/>
It doesn&#39;t look like the jetty jars are actually needed by cxf-rt-transports-http, and the servlet-api spec should have the &quot;provided&quot; scope since it will already be bundled with the servlet container.  Could we fix this or are they needed for some reason?
  </td>
