                <tr id="issuerow12370258" rel="12370258" data-issuekey="CXF-690" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-690" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-690">CXF-690</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                durable subscriptions is not set in JMS transport
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Willem Jiang
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Willem Jiang
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Willem Jiang
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 25/May/07 10:52 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 29/Aug/07 02:04 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 28/May/07 07:48 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.0-RC            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Transports            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I started working on cxf jms systems against Sonic MQ and have a question about JMS durable subscription.<br/>
<br/>
 <br/>
<br/>
In the system test jms_test.wsdl file, a durable subscriber name is defined.<br/>
<br/>
 <br/>
<br/>
    &lt;service name=&quot;HelloWorldService&quot;&gt;<br/>
<br/>
           &lt;port binding=&quot;tns:HelloWorldPortBinding&quot; name=&quot;HelloWorldPort&quot;&gt;<br/>
<br/>
               &lt;jms:address<br/>
<br/>
                   jndiConnectionFactoryName=&quot;ConnectionFactory&quot;<br/>
<br/>
                   jndiDestinationName=&quot;dynamicQueues/test.jmstransport.text&quot;&gt;<br/>
<br/>
                   &lt;jms:JMSNamingProperty name=&quot;java.naming.factory.initial&quot; value=&quot;org.apache.activemq.jndi.ActiveMQInitialContextFactory&quot;/&gt;<br/>
<br/>
                   &lt;jms:JMSNamingProperty name=&quot;java.naming.provider.url&quot; value=&quot;tcp://localhost:61500&quot;/&gt;<br/>
<br/>
               &lt;/jms:address&gt;<br/>
<br/>
           <br/>
<br/>
               &lt;jms:server durableSubscriberName=&quot;CXF_subscriber&quot;/&gt;<br/>
<br/>
           &lt;/port&gt;<br/>
<br/>
&lt;/service&gt;<br/>
 <br/>
<br/>
It seems a durable subscription will be created by client, according to the line 469 in the file \rt\transports\jms\src\main\java\org\apache\cxf\transport\jms\JMSSessionFactory.java<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
When I ran the test with this service, the test ran fine, but I didn&#39;t see any created durable subscriptions from Sonic management console. Can you view durable subscriptions when testing ActiveMQ?  <br/>
<br/>
The error was reproduced in ActiveMQ. <br/>

  </td>
