                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Current CXF provides a JMX API to star or stop the managed endpoint.<br/>
This command line tool can make the user more easy to start or stop the server side endpoint.<br/>
<br/>
The command line tool option could be <br/>
<br/>
Managed Console for CXF<br/>
	 Valid options<br/>
-j [--jmx] arg 		 the jmxServerURL that need to connet mbean server <br/>
			 the default value is service:jmx:rmi:///jndi/rmi://localhost:1099/jmxrmi<br/>
-p [--port] arg 	 the port name of the managed endpoint<br/>
			 the arg is the Qname of port<br/>
-s [--service] arg 	 the service name of the managed endpoint<br/>
			 the arg format the Qname of service<br/>
-o [--operation] {list|start|stop|restart} 	 call the jmx functions<br/>
			 list: show all the managed endpoints&#39; objectNames and attributs <br/>
			 start: start the endpoint with the --port and --service arguments<br/>
			 stop: stop the endpoint with the --port and --service arguments<br/>
			 restart: restart the endpoint with the --port and --service arguments 
  </td>
