</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      <br/>
The JAX-WS RI uses a 202 Accepted message in &quot;chunked&quot; form to respond to a OneWay message.   According to the WSI BP, that is allowed.   However, CXF seems to think it&#39;s a partial response message and tries to parse it as XML, thus throwing an exception.<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
Response from RI:<br/>
<br/>
HTTP/1.1 202 Accepted <br/>
Server: Apache-Coyote/1.1 <br/>
Transfer-Encoding: chunked <br/>
Date: Wed, 25 Jul 2007 02:27:30 GMT <br/>
 <br/>
0 <br/>
<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
