</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        CXF-535                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Tested on Tomcat 5.5.23, but probably independent of environment
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      The service listing generated by the CXFServlet at the context root, e.g. &quot;http://localhost/webservice/&quot;, contains links missing the last character if called without the final &#39;/&#39; (i.e. as &quot;http://localhost/webservice&quot;), which has been tested with Tomcat and most likely is possible in most containers. See attached screenshots.<br/>
<br/>
Without having seen the code, I would assume the final character is stripped to avoid the problem described in CXF-535, but it seems this also happens if it is *not* a slash.
  </td>
